MCQ 3.145
A 72-year-old woman attends the Emergency Department with dysuria, frequency
and pneumaturia with bacilluria. One month earlier she was in hospital and a pelvic
abscess was drained. Which one of the following is the most likely underlying cause
of her current problem?
A pyosalpinx.
A tubo-ovarian abscess.
. Urinary tract infection.
. Acolovesical fistula.
lleal Crohn disease.
MOOR >
MCQ 3.146
A 50-year-old man is concerned because his 79-year-old father has recently been
diagnosed with carcinoma of the prostate after a blood test and biopsy. He asks
what is the natural history of this cancer, the place of transurethral or radical surgery,
what blood test can be performed, how the tumour spreads, and whether hormone
treatment is indicated. In responding to his queries, which one of the following is the
most appropriate advice?','{"A":"Itis screened for by a specific acid phosphatase blood test.","B":"It metastasises to groin lymph nodes.","C":"Itis most effectively managed by transurethral resection.","D":"It. can, in the early stages be cured by radical surgery.","E":"Itis treated with tamoxifen if disseminated.\n\nMCQ 3.147\n\nA 24-year-old male presents to the Emergency Department complaining of\npersisting and severe abdominal pain radiating from the loin to the groin. On clinical\nexamination there is no tenderness over the site of the pain and no other positive\nfindings. A specimen of urine, which he has brought in, is obviously blood stained. He\nrequests an injection of pethidine for relief of pain. Which one of the following is the\nmost appropriate next step in management?\n\nArrange a plain film and computed tomograph (CT) as soon as possible.\n\nExamine a freshly voided specimen of urine.\n\n. Prescribe pethidine and hyoscine butylbromide (Buscopan®) tablets and review\nnext day.\n\n. Administer 100mg pethidine intramuscularly and review in four hours.\n\nArrange admission to hospital for investigation.\n\nOR\n\nmoO\n\nad ''"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.145","duplicate_group_id":"exact-98c642904ea5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"755a43f17c251c70f994","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":288,"source_qid":"3.145"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"755a43f17c251c70f994","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relativ