MCQ 3.148
A 64-year-old man with a three-month history of increasing frequency, nocturia
and dysuria undergoes a cystoscopy. Instrumentation is difficult. Six hours after the
procedure he has a rigor and develops a temperature of 40°C. Which one of the
following is the most likely explanation for this complication?','{"A":"Acute pyelonephritis.","B":"Rupture of the bladder.","C":"Gram-negative bacteraemia.","D":"Rupture of the prostatic urethra.","E":"Rupture of the membranous urethra.\n\nMCQ 3.149\n\nA 25-year-old patient is being staged for further management of a seminoma which\npresented as a lump in the left testis. Involvement of which one of the following lymph\nnode groups by lymphatic spread would indicate the worst prognosis?\n\nA. Cervical.\n\nB. Mediastinal.\n\nC. Retroperitoneal.\nD. Inguinal.\n\nE. Femoral canal.\n\nMCQ 3.150\n\nAn 80-year-old man with controlled congestive cardiac failure presents with backache\nand is discovered to have spinal metastases from prostatic carcinoma. Which one of\nthe following is the best initial treatment?\n\nTestosterone.\nStilboestrol.\n\n. Chemotherapy.\nOrchidectomy.\n\nRadical prostatectomy.\n\nMOQ2>\n\nMCQ 3.151\n\nA 66-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department in distress with severe\nlower abdominal pain. He has been unable to void for the past twelve hours, has\nbeen constipated for the past two days, and gives a two-year history of increasing\ndifficulty passing urine with a poor stream. He has to get up 6-8 times at night to pass\nurine. Which one of the following is the most appropriate initial management?\n\nAdminister a rectal laxative suppository.\n\nAdminister intramuscular neostigmine methylsulfate.\n\n. Administer 10mg morphine and 10mg of hyoscine butylbromide intramuscularly.\n. Insert an indwelling urethral catheter into the bladder.\n\nArrange suprapubic drainage of the bladder.\n\nMOOR >"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.148","duplicate_group_id":"exact-8ad23d598079","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a94ab5bd30f749ebe2c6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":289,"source_qid":"3.148"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"a94ab5bd30f749ebe2c6","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":289,"source_qid":"3.148","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"icy\nvic\nJse\nen\nsks\nny,\nne\nhe\nWw\nSecti Adi alth and Aged |\nAustralian Medical Council\nfer\nMCQ 3.148\nA 64-year-old man with a three-month history of increasing frequency, nocturia\nand dysuria undergoes a cystoscopy. Instrumentation is difficult. Six hours after the\nprocedure he has a rigor and develops a temperature of 40°C. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely explanation for this complication?","options":{"A":"Acute pyelonephritis.","B":"Rupture of the bladder.","C":"Gram-negative bacteraemia.","D":"Rupture of the prostatic urethra.","E":"Rupture of the membranous urethra.\n\nMCQ 3.149\n\nA 25-year-old patient is being staged for further management of a seminoma which\npresented as a lump in the left testis. Involvement of which one of the following lymph\nnode groups by lymphatic spread would indicate the worst prognosis?\n\nA. Cervical.\n\nB. Mediastinal.\n\nC. Retroperitoneal.\nD. Inguinal.\n\nE. Femoral canal.\n\nMCQ 3.150\n\nAn 80-year-old man with controlled congestive cardiac failure presents with backache\nand is discovered to have spinal metastases from prostatic carcinoma. Which one of\nthe following is the best initial treatment?\n\nTestosterone.\nStilboestrol.\n\n. Chemotherapy.\nOrchidectomy.\n\nRadical prostatectomy.\n\nMOQ2>\n\nMCQ 3.151\n\nA 66-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department in distress with severe\nlower abdominal pain. He has been unable to void for the past twelve hours, has\nbeen constipated for the past two days, and gives a two-year history of increasing\ndifficulty passing urine with a poor stream. He has to get up 6-8 times at night to pass\nurine. Which one of the following is the most appropriate initial management?\n\nAdminister a rectal laxative suppository.\n\nAdminister intramuscular neostigmine methylsulfate.\n\n. Administer 10mg morphine and 10mg of hyoscine butylbromide intramuscularly.\n. Insert an indwelling urethral catheter into the bladder.\n\nArrange suprapubic drainage of the bladder.\n\nMOOR >"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"8ad23d5980797dfbf0494d43bf47869893fc63c5","duplicate_group_id":"exact-8ad23d598079","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a94ab5bd30f749ebe2c6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":289,"source_qid":"3.148"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=exclud