INSERT INTO canonical_records (record_id,source_file,source_page,domain,stem,options_json,source_answer,source_explanation,provenance_json,visual_asset,visual_url,options_mode,current_answer,current_answer_status,current_evidence_json,currentness_risk,record_json,active_quiz,import_version,imported_at) VALUES ('fcab781645bb118556c9','96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf','291','Mixed/Unclassified','Australian Medical Council
Section 3— Adult Health and Aged Care
. Transurethral resection of the prostate.
External beam radiotherapy.
. Radical prostatectomy.
. Androgen deprivation with gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GRH).
Orchidectomy.
UNS BO ee a
MCQ 3.156
A 62-year-old man presents acutely with urgency of micturition for the last three days.
On neurologic examination, his cranial nerves and upper limbs are normal. There is
weakness of hip flexion bilaterally, his knee and ankle jerks are brisk and the plantar
responses are extensor. Touch and pinprick are impaired below the inguinal ligament
bilaterally. Joint position sense and vibration sense are reduced in his legs. Which one
of the following is the most likely cause of his symptoms?','{"A":"Compression of the spinal cord at the T10 vertebral level.","B":"Compression of the spinal cord by an L1-L2 intervertebral disc protrusion.","C":"Subacute combined degeneration of the cord (B,,deficiency).","D":"Syringomyelia.","E":"Lumbosacral spondylolisthesis.\n\nMCQ 3.157\n\nA 40-year-old woman, who has a history of chronic domestic violence, presents with\na painless lower abdominal swelling which she has noted for the past month. She is\nfound to have a non-tender urinary bladder, enlarged to the level of the umbilicus,\nconfirmed on abdominal ultrasound. General examination and systems review are\notherwise normal. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nA bladder neoplasm.\n\nPregnancy.\n\n. Acute retention of urine.\n\nChronic retention of urine.\n\nA neuropathic bladder with an incompetent urethral sphincter.\n\nTMOORP>\n\nMCQ 3.158\n\nA 32-year-old man with a testicular neoplasm has para-aortic lymph node\ninvolvement more than 15cm diameter on clinical examination, confirmed by\nabdominal computed tomograph (CT) estimation. Which one of the following\ntreatment options is the most appropriate?\n\nRadiation therapy to the para-aortic nodes.\n\nChemoradiotherapy alone.\n\n. Surgical excision of nodes plus chemotherapy, with delayed orchidectomy.\n\n. Orchidectomy plus chemoradiotherapy and delayed surgery for residual nodes.\nRadiation therapy to the primary tumour and the para-aortic lymph nodes.\n\nMOQR?>\n\n273"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.156","duplicate_group_id":"exact-01523c1c1a48","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"fcab781645bb118556c9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":291,"source_qi