MCQ 3.164
| In an acute emergency with exsanguinating blood loss, if blood has to be given
immediately without full laboratory cross-matching, which one of the following is best
to give?','{"A":"Group O RhD -ve.","B":"Group O RhD +ve.","C":"Group AB RhD -ve.","D":"Group AB RhD +ve.","E":"Group A RhD -ve.\n| MCQ 3.165\n/ A 45-year-old man with Type 2 diabetes mellitus well controlled on diet who is on\nsj | normal unrestricted intake of food and fluids, has studies performed on a twenty-\nfour hour urine collection sample. Which one of the following twenty-four hour urinary\n/ output findings is significantly outside the normal range?\n| A. Water 1.5L.\nB. Sodium 80mmol.\n| C. Potassium 80mmol.\n| D. Protein 500mg.\n/ E. Total titratable acid 150mmol.\nq MCQ 3.166\n/ . A 25-year-old labourer was trapped on a building site causing soft tissue crush injury to\n| trunk and limbs. He was extricated after six hours and taken by ambulance to hospital.\nP He had generalised bruising and abrasions, without significant open wounds; and had\n7 widespread muscle and soft tissue tenderness over trunk and limbs. Pulse was 110/\ni min and regular, BP 110/70mmHg, temperature 36.7°C. He was unable to provide a\nurine specimen; urethral catheterisation yielded 30mL of dark urine positive for blood.\nj X-ray of chest, limbs and abdomen showed no bony injuries. His electrocardiogram\n(ECG) showed the pattern illustrated over a 15-minute period (ECG A and ECG B).\n| The ECG changes demonstrate evidence of which one of the following electrolyte\n» | abnormalities?\n| Bet 4 X Neh K \\ K fo tectscccans per\nB) i ‘ a Varaty br VIN I $B 190 428/€89 11 5-80\n| a ARAL prerrisesnhels \\\nmy mp\n: memes ceri reat a NNN VEZ}\nGi\nBle ; j clingy eta Iaacd bh\nmee ‘| : |\nSII ert eee\nECGA ECG B\n! 279"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.164","duplicate_group_id":"exact-9a4acd8938bb","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e142c682438339c14818","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.H