MCQ 3.168
The patient shown in the illustration has been receiving
intravenous fluids and nil by mouth for four weeks to manage
a duodenal fistula developing after partial gastrectomy, done
in a rural hospital. He has been transferred to a tertiary referral
intensive care unit because of the development of a florid skin
rash as illustrated. Which one of the following agents given
intravenously is likely to be most helpful in his treatment?
Iron.
Zinc.
. Copper.
Manganese.
lodide.
MCQ 3.169
MOQOP>
A 69-year-old woman is brought to the Emergency Department with drowsiness and
diarrhoea over the past four days. She lives alone. She is known to have diabetes,
hypertension and ischaemic heart disease, and epilepsy. Her daily medications
include glibenclamide 10mg, metoprolol 100mg, hydrochorothiazide 25mg, phenytoin
300mg and aspirin 100mg.
She is drowsy on examination but responds to painful stimuli. Her BP is 120/70mmHg,
pulse is 110/min and the rest of the examination does not reveal any abnormality.
Her urine shows ketones + and glucose ++++.
