Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
MCQ 3.180
On mass chest X-ray examination, a 45-year-old woman appears to have a solitary
round pulmonary metastasis. Physical examination is normal. Which one of the
following investigations is most likely to locate the primary tumour?
. Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy.
Lower gastrointestinal endoscopy.
. Abdominal computed tomography (CT).
. Mammography.
Thyroid isotope scan.
MO OW’ s
MCQ 3.181
A 60-year-old woman presents after an episode of
sharp pain under her right costal margin. The pain was
constant and lasted several hours before resolving
spontaneously. The woman enjoys good health and
does not take any medications. She has a twenty
pack-year smoking history and drinks about two
glasses of wine most days. The physical examination
is normal. An abdominal ultrasound examination is
performed andis pictured. Which one of the following
