Patients with acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS) are prone to infections
with a variety of infecting organisms, some of which constitute AIDS-defining illnesses.
Which one of the following infections is least likely to be associated with AIDS?
. Haemophilus influenzae meningitis.
. Cytomegalovirus retinitis.
. Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia.
. Candida oesophagitis.
. Cryptosporidial enteritis.
MCQ 3.183
The acceptable maximal cold ischaemic storage time is shortest in which one of the
following vascularised allografts?
. Hepatic transplantation.
. Renal transplantation.
. Pancreatic transplantation.
. Cardiac transplantation.
. Pulmonary transplantation.
MCQ 3.184
A 30-year-old man with end-stage renal disease secondary to diabetes is about to
undergo living related kidney transplantation. The donor is one of his two living siblings
(all siblings have the same parents). Which one of the following is the approximate
likelihood of a two haplotype match from such a transplant between siblings?
. 5% (1 in 20, probability .05).
. 25% (1 in 4, probability .25).
. 50% (1 in 2, probability .50).
. 75% (3 in 4, probability .75).
. 90% (9 in 10, probability .90).
MCQ 3.185
A 40-year-old patient is on a longterm followup program having undergone a renal
transplant 10 years earlier. The only medication he takes regularly is cyclosporin. He is
otherwise in good health with stable renal function. From which one of the following
conditions is he most at risk of dying?','{"A":"Renal transplant rejection.","B":"Renal failure.","C":"Stroke.","D":"Myocardial infarction.","E":"Malignancy."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[311],"source_qid":"3.182","duplicate_group_id":"exact-87974389f3d2","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a88578d8b94cad9cfd02","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":311,"source_qid":"3.182"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"a88578d8b94cad9cfd02","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":311,"supporting_pages":[311],"source_qid":"3.182","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"MCQ 3.182\nPatients with acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS) are prone to infections\nwith a variety of infecting organisms, some of which constitute AIDS-defining illnesses.\nWhich one of the following infections is least likely to be associated with AIDS?\n. Haemophilus influenzae meningitis.\n. Cytomegalovirus retinitis.\n. Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia.\n. Candida oesophagitis.\n. Cryptosporidial enteritis.\nMCQ 3.183\nThe acceptable maximal cold ischaemic storage time is shortest in which one of the\nfollowing vascularised allografts?\n. Hepatic transplantation.\n. Renal transplantation.\n. Pancreatic transplantation.\n. Cardiac transplantation.\n. Pulmonary transplantation.\nMCQ 3.184\nA 30-year-old man with end-stage renal disease secondary to diabetes is about t