to speak, has difficulty breathing and is acutely distressed. Which one of the following
should be done immediately?','{"A":"Insert an oral airway.","B":"Attempt endotracheal intubation.","C":"Apply forceful upper abdominal compression.","D":"Perform cricothyroid membrane needling.","E":"Provide oxygen by facemask.\n\nMCQ 3.187\n\nA 20-year-old man develops an enterocutaneous (small bowel) fistula after an\nabdominal gunshot wound. He is transferred to a tertiary referral hospital two weeks\nafter the injury. The output from the fistula has been 1800mL daily for the past three\ndays. Which one of the following is the most important initial step in management?\n\nA."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.186","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b23d23f46a5c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b517b182168810ff3758","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":313,"source_qid":"3.186"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"b517b182168810ff3758","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":313,"source_qid":"3.186","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Ausiralian Medical Council\nSection 3— Adult Health and Aged Care\nMCQ 3.186\nAn adult resident of a nursing home is found choking on a lump of meat. He is unable\nto speak, has difficulty breathing and is acutely distressed. Which one of the following\nshould be done immediately?","options":{"A":"Insert an oral airway.","B":"Attempt endotracheal intubation.","C":"Apply forceful upper abdominal compression.","D":"Perform cricothyroid membrane needling.","E":"Provide oxygen by facemask.\n\nMCQ 3.187\n\nA 20-year-old man develops an enterocutaneous (small bowel) fistula after an\nabdominal gunshot wound. He is transferred to a tertiary referral hospital two weeks\nafter the injury. The output from the fistula has been 1800mL daily for the past three\ndays. Which one of the following is the most important initial step in management?\n\nA."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"b23d23f46a5ccf8245284649f1c234df2a07bad1","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b23d23f46a5c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b517b182168810ff3758","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":313,"source_qid":"3.186"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version