MCQ 3.200
A 25-year-old woman presents with a troublesome mucopurulent vaginal discharge. —
On clinical examination she has a large cervical ‘erosion’ which is draining a large ~
amount of thick mucoid material. Pap smear tests have been done regularly since she
was 15 years old and have always been normal. The last such smear was performed
three months ago. Which one of the following would be the most appropriate next step
in management?
. Reassure her no treatment is required.
Oral cephalexin (Keflex®).
. Colposcopic examination of the cervix.
. Cone biopsy.
Cauterisation of the cervix.
Mm OC) oF >
MCQ 3.201
A 34-year-old woman, who has been taking the oral contraceptive pill (OCP)
Microgynon 30%, is found to have a BP of 160/100mmHg when she attends for a repeat
prescription. She indicates to you that she will wish to cease the OCP in six months to
enable her to conceive. Which one of the following is the most appropriate advice?','{"A":"Continue the OCP unchanged, but add methyldopa as a hypotensive agent, as\nthis could be continued during a subsequent pregnancy.","B":"Change the OCP to a preparation with a lower oestrogen dose, such as\nMicrogynon 20°.","C":"Cease the OCP and commence hypotensive treatment with methyldopa.","D":"Cease the OCP, use condoms for contraception, and reassess the BP in three\nmonths.","E":"Cease the OCP and commence treatment with an angiotensin-converting\nenzyme (ACE) inhibitor, as this can be continued during pregnancy.\n\nres\nMCQ 3.202\n\nA 45-year-old woman complains of a series of heavy irregular periods. Six months\npreviously her menstrual pattern had been quite normal. On physical examination\nno abnormality was detected and cervical smear was negative. Her haemoglobin\nvalue was 115g/L (115-165). Which one of the following is the most common cause of\nthis type of menorrhagia?\n\n. Endometrial carcinoma.\nAnovulatory cycles.\n\n. Submucous fibroids.\n\n. Endometrial polyps.\nAdenomyosis.\n\nMmOoQ2 >"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.200","duplicate_group_id":"exact-14191a64089a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5ebbeac10c630530b44f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":320,"source_qid":"3.200"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"5ebbeac10c630530b44f","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questi