MCQ 3.205
A 24-year-old woman, who has not conceived after two years of unprotected
= intercourse, presents because she is concerned she may have endometriosis. This
concern has arisen because she has a friend who was recently diagnosed with this
condition. Which one of the following symptom profiles is most likely if endometriosis is
ns actually present in this woman?','{"A":"Dysmenorrhoea from the time of the menarche.","B":"Dyspareunia.","C":"Menorrhagia.","D":"Mid-cycle vaginal bleeding.","E":"No abnormal bleeding or pain."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.203","duplicate_group_id":"exact-f29ad1e3ff99","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"efc778f90015720b72bc","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":321,"source_qid":"3.203"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"efc778f90015720b72bc","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":321,"source_qid":"3.203","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"eS eee Council\nMCQ 3.203\nJe. A couple in their mid-twenties have decided to use the ‘Rhythm Method’ (calendar\nje calculation) as their contraceptive method, abstaining from sexual intercourse at\nqe the time a pregnancy would otherwise be likely to result. They are keen to avoid a\nEXO| pregnancy for the next two years. The woman has charted her cycles for the last\n3 twelve months and these have varied in length between 26 and 29 days. Which one\nof the following abstinence periods would be the correct advice?\nFrom day 4 to day 17.\nFrom day 6 to day 17.\nFrom day 8 to day 19.\nFrom day 10 to day 19.\nFrom day 12 to day 19.\nPSO S\nMCQ 3.204\nP) A 28-year-old woman with primary infertility presents to her general practitioner\nat because of secondary amenorrhoea of 12 months duration. Which one of the\nto following hormone assays, if the result is clearly markedly elevated, would indicate\n38 that a pregnancy has already occurred?\nOs Serum oestradiol (E2).\nSerum progesterone.\n. Serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH).\n. Serum luteinising hormone (LH).\nSerum prolactin (PRL).\nas\nMOORP>\nMCQ 3.205\nA 24-year-old woman, who has not conceived after two years of unprotected\n= intercourse, presents because she is concerned she may have endometriosis. This\nconcern has arisen because she has a friend who was recently diagnosed with this\ncondition. Which one of the following symptom profiles is most likely if endometriosis is\nns actually present in this woman?","options":{"A":"Dysmenorrhoea from the time of the menarche.","B":"Dyspareunia.","C":"Menorrhagia.","D":"Mid-cycle vaginal bleeding.","E":"No abnormal bleeding or pain."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["contracept","duration","pregnan"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"f29ad1e3ff9984c08973858e1eb50763d9b29550","duplicate_group_id":"exact-f29ad1e3ff99","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"efc778f90015720b72bc","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":321,"source_qid":"3.203"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.sou