MCQ 3.210
A 50-year-old woman, whose last menstrual period occurred at the age of 49 years,
had an episode of vaginal bleeding of three days duration, two weeks ago. Just prior
to the bleeding, she had noticed a reduction in the extent of her hot flushes and
some breast enlargement. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of this
bleeding?','{"A":"Carcinoma of the cervix.","B":"Carcinoma of the endometrium.","C":"Atrophic vaginitis.","D":"An episode of ovarian follicular activity.","E":"Cystic endometrial hyperplasia.\n\nMCQ 3.211\n\nA 49-year-old woman comes to see you because she has not had a period for the\nlast 11 months. Prior to that time her periods were regular and normal. You arranged\nfor her follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and oestradiol (E2) levels to be measured.\nWhich one of the patterns below would be most likely to be found, assuming she has\nreached menopause?\n\nLow FSH and low E2.\n\nLow FSH and normal E2.\n\n. Normal FSH and low E2.\nNormal FSH and normal E2.\nHigh FSH and low E2.\n\nMOQR>\n\nMCQ 3.212\n\nA 40-year-old woman, who has previously had a Filshie clip sterilisation, complains of\nexcessively heavy but regular periods. She is known to have multiple uterine fibroids\nand her uterus is enlarged to that of a 12-week pregnancy. Her Pap smear is normal,\nand her haemoglobin is 93g/L. She had a dilatation and curettage performed six\nmonths ago, but this has not improved her symptoms and did not define an underlying\ncause. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOral progestogen therapy from day 14-24 of her cycle.\n\nProstaglandin synthetase inhibitor (e.g. Ponstan®) during the bleeding episodes.\n. Myomectomy.\n\nEndometrial ablation.\n\nTotal abdominal hysterectomy.\n\nMOQOP>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.210","duplicate_group_id":"exact-800b7f877954","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7af3f55ec05e701c1d08","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":323,"source_qid":"3.210"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"7af3f55ec05e701c1d08","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":323,"source_qid":"3.210","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Medical Cc\nth and\n. Laparoscopic ovarian drilling.\n. Ovulation induction with gonadotrophins.\n. Donor insemination.\n. Treatment with metformin.\n. In vitro fertilisation.\nMCQ 3.210\nA 50-year-old woman, whose last menstrual period occurred at the age of 49 years,\nhad an episode of vaginal bleeding of three days duration, two weeks ago. Just prior\nto the bleeding, she had noticed a reduction in the extent of her hot flushes and\nsome breast enlargement. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of this\nbleeding?","options":{"A":"Carcinoma of the cervix.","B":"Carcinoma of the endometrium.","C":"Atrophic vaginitis.","D":"An episode of ovarian follicular activity.","E":"Cystic endometrial hyperplasia.\n\nMCQ 3.211\n\nA 49-year-old woman comes to see you because she has not had a period for the\nlast 11 months. Prior to that time her periods were regular and normal. You arranged\nfor her follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and oestradiol (E2) levels to be measured.\nWhich one of the patterns below would be most likely to be found, assuming she has\nreached menopause?\n\nLow FSH and low E2.\n\nLow FSH and normal E2.\n\n. Normal FSH and low E2.\nNormal FSH and normal E2.\nHigh FSH and low E2.\n\nMOQR>\n\nMCQ 3.212\n\nA 40-year-old woman, who has previously had a Filshie clip sterilisation, complains of\nexcessively heavy but regular periods. She is known to have multiple uterine fibroids\nand her uterus is enlarged to that of a 12-week pregnancy. Her Pap smear is normal,\nand her haemoglobin is 93g/L. She had a dilatation and curettage performed six\nmonths ago, but this has not improved her symptoms and did not define an underlying\ncause. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOral progestogen therapy from day 14-24 of her cycle.\n\nProstaglandin synthetase inhibitor (e.g. Ponstan®) during the bleeding episodes.\n. Myomectomy.\n\nEndometrial ablation.\n\nTotal abdominal hysterectomy.\n\nMOQOP>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","duration","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"800b7f8779546895ab5640dd42e3b0d17ff373c5","duplicate_group_id":"exact-800b7f877954","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7af3f55ec05e701c1d08","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":323,"source_qid":"3.210"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.