INSERT INTO canonical_records (record_id,source_file,source_page,domain,stem,options_json,source_answer,source_explanation,provenance_json,visual_asset,visual_url,options_mode,current_answer,current_answer_status,current_evidence_json,currentness_risk,record_json,active_quiz,import_version,imported_at) VALUES ('63ae72d9b285aeec2b20','96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf','327','Mixed/Unclassified','Section 3— Adult Health and Aged |
. Gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) agonist injections.
. Norethisterone from day 5 to day 25 of the cycle.
. Medroxy progesterone acetate from day 15 to day 25 of the cycle.
. Danazol 400mg/day continuously.
. The combined oestrogen/progestogen oral contraceptive pill (OCP).
MCQ 3.223
A 25-year-old woman usually takes her oral contraceptive pill (ethinyl oestradiol 30ug,
levonorgestrel 150g) each night at about 10pm. She presents at 6pm one day, and
indicates she forgot to take her pill the evening before and wants advice as to what
she should do. She had sexual intercourse last night and is now on day 27 of the
cycle. She is due to take her last hormone tablet tonight and then start the first of her
seven lactose tablets tomorrow night. Which one of the following would be the most
appropriate advice?','{"A":"Take her next contraceptive pill tonight and forget about the one she missed.","B":"Take a double dose (two tablets) now, then continue the original course, taking\nthe next tablet tomorrow night.","C":"Take the missed pill now, and then continue the original course, taking the next\ntablet in four hours time.","D":"Stop the current course of contraceptive pills, and start the next course of hormone\ntablets in five days time.","E":"Take Postinor® (750ug levonorgestrel) now, and in 12 hours time, then resume the\noriginal contraceptive pill.\n\nMCQ 3.224\n\nA 28-year-old woman with primary infertility presents with secondary amenorrhoea\nof twelve months duration. Which one of the following hormone assay results, if\nabnormal, would be of most value in predicting that a poor response to ovulation-\ninduction therapy is likely?\n\nSerum oestradiol.\n\nSerum thyroxine.\n\n. Serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH).\nSerum luteinising hormone.\n\nSerum prolactin.\n\nMOQ >\n\nMCQ 3.225\nA 48-year-old woman is seeking advice concerning the use of hormone replacement\ntherapy (HRT) when she reaches the menopause. She is still having regular menstrual\ncycles and has had no hot flushes or other problems as yet. She is particularly worried\nabout Alzheimer disease (AD), as her mother developed this at the age of 70 years\n\nand is now confined to living in a nursing home. Which one of the following would be\nthe most appropriate advice concerning Alzheimer disease and the use of HRT?\n\nAustralian Medical Council"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.223","duplicate_group_id":"exact-61f439fb420b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"63ae72d9b285aeec2b20","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","sou