pill.\n\nMCQ 3.224\n\nA 28-year-old woman with primary infertility presents with secondary amenorrhoea\nof twelve months duration. Which one of the following hormone assay results, if\nabnormal, would be of most value in predicting that a poor response to ovulation-\ninduction therapy is likely?\n\nSerum oestradiol.\n\nSerum thyroxine.\n\n. Serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH).\nSerum luteinising hormone.\n\nSerum prolactin.\n\nMOQ >\n\nMCQ 3.225\nA 48-year-old woman is seeking advice concerning the use of hormone replacement\ntherapy (HRT) when she reaches the menopause. She is still having regular menstrual\ncycles and has had no hot flushes or other problems as yet. She is particularly worried\nabout Alzheimer disease (AD), as her mother developed this at the age of 70 years\n\nand is now confined to living in a nursing home. Which one of the following would be\nthe most appropriate advice concerning Alzheimer disease and the use of HRT?\n\nAustralian Medical Council"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age","contracept"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"61f439fb420badab1d5f2e1b0cd30f3d877a02ba","duplicate_group_id":"exact-61f439fb420b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"63ae72d9b285aeec2b20","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":327,"source_qid":"3.223"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem