MCQ 3.229
A S-year-old boy presents with a three-day history of bilateral knee and ankle pain.
On examination he is afebrile, his joints are tender without swelling, inflammation or
synovial thickening. There is a fullrange of joint movements. He has. a palpable purpuric
rash on his legs and buttocks with some ecchymotic lesions around his ankles. He has
. no lymphadenopathy nor hepatosplenomegaly, and heart sounds are normal.
Full blood count, blood urea, electrolytes and liver function tests are normal. ESR is
T1mm/hr (2-15). Which one of the following is a known complication of this boy’s
condition?','{"A":"Pleurisy.","B":"Fasciitis.","C":"Nephritis.","D":"Thrombocytopenia.","E":"Diabetes mellitus.\n,\nMCQ 3.230\nA 5-year-old boy has an itchy rash all over his body which has increased over the past\ntwo days. The child also has a runny nose, mild cough and a reduced appetite for the\nlast four days. On examination he has a temperature of 38°C, pulse rate 120/min and |\na generalised urticarial rash. Which one of the following is the most likely explanation\nfor his rash?\nA. Viral upper respiratory tract infection (URTI).\nB. Allergic reaction to food.\nC. Measles infection.\nD. Infected eczema.\n\\ E. Drug reaction.\na ecsesssesseseennsnennsrnnnssnssent\nMCQ 3.231\nA child is noted to have developed the\nappearance illustrated in the fingers of | i ae i\nboth hands. In which one of the following | ——<\n\\ conditions is this clinical sign most likely to } ES ee\nbe found? I\nA. Tetralogy of Fallot.\nB. Ventricular septal defect.\nC. Chronic asthma.\nD. Chronic hepatitis B infection.\nf E. Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). in\n|\n313"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.229","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7023d96074bb","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5fb7d8181f7216b9e974","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":331,"source_qid":"3.229"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"5fb7d8181f7216b9e974","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pd