: : gf
MCQ 3.244
A 10-year-old girl presents with a two-month history of lethargy and a swelling in her
‘ neck. On specific questioning she has had normal bowel habits, normal appetite, no
i weight loss and no vomiting. On examination her weight is on the 50th percentile,
height is on the 25th percentile, BP 90/45mmbg, physical examination is normal except
for a smooth diffuse swelling of the thyroid gland.The following are her investigation
results:
, Urea, electrolytes, liver function tests & full blood count normal
Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) *>100mlu/L (<5)
