. Now.
. In four weeks.
. In eight weeks.
. When weight >4kg.
. When weight >5kg.
MCQ 3.253
A newborn baby has respiratory distress. She was born by elective Caesarean section
delivery at 38 weeks gestation. Apgar scores were 7 at 1 minute and 9 at 5 minutes.
Birth weight was 3180gm. Respiratory difficulty commenced at one hour of age. She
i was placed in 30% oxygen. At two hours of age she is tachypnoeic with a respiratory
| rate of 30/minute with some subcostal recession. Chest is clear to auscultation, heart
sounds are normal. Pulse oximetry reads 91% breathing 30% oxygen. Which one of the
following is the most urgent next step in management?','{"A":"Commence antibiotics.","B":"Increase inspired oxygen concentration.","C":"Chest X-ray.","D":"Insert an umbilical arterial line.","E":"Insert an umbilical venous catheter.\n\nMCQ 3.254\n\nA baby is born to a woman who has previously been healthy except for mild\nhypertension. She has had two previous children and had spontaneous rupture of\nmembranes and onset of labour at term. She received pain relief with an intramuscular\ninjection of 10mg morphine two hours before the delivery. After an uncomplicated\nvacuum delivery the baby is slow to breathe with an Apgar score of 4 at 1 minute.\nWhich one of the following is the most important next step in the baby’s care?\n\nA. Intramuscular naloxone.\n\nB. Oxygen by nasal catheter.\n\nC. Umbilical venous 8.4% sodium bicarbonate.\nD. Bag and mask ventilation.\n\nE. Intubation.\n\nMCQ 3.255\n\nA3-year-old boy is admitted with a one-week history of increasing generalised swelling\nand periorbital puffiness following a respiratory infection two weeks previously. On\nexamination, he has generalised oedema, with ascites and marked scrotal oedema.\nHe is normotensive.\n\nUrine testing shows 4+ protein, there is no glycosuria or haematuria. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely cause for his presentation?\n\nIgA nephropathy.\n\nAcute glomerulonephritis.\n\n. Reflux nephropathy.\n\nInterstitial nephritis.\n\nNephrotic syndrome.\n\nMOOR>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.253","duplicate_group_id":"exact-67d0945b18ad","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"29ab8e946f3d084b1655","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":340,"source_qid":"3.253"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-