become less responsive. She also has noted that he has had several episodes of
; suddenly jerking forward when being cuddled and these events occur in clusters of
three to four at a time. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in
: management?','{"A":"Arrange an electroencephalogram (EEG).","B":"Sodium valproate.","C":"Arrange a full neurodevelopmental assessment by a psychologist.","D":"Repeat the karyotype as this is inconsistent with a diagnosis of Down syndrome.","E":"Explain his presentation is a form of self-stimulatory behaviour not requiring any\ntreatment.\nSetlists eet ssa ansnnscens msm\nMCQ 3.257\nA 2-year-old child presents because his 4 ne Bae ih\nparents have noted that for several months a aed\nhe has had an intermittent limp affecting his oe — =\ni leftleg. They are unsure whether this is painful ev: TM\nor not. Examination when he is standing ae “g\nsuggests his left leg is shorter than the other , a st\n| and he has some limitation of abduction of oe Jag\n; his left hip. His hip X-ray is shown. Which one Maa\nof the following is the most likely diagnosis? }\nA. Developmental dysplasia of the hip.\nB. Perthes disease.\nC. Chronic juvenile arthritis.\nD. Slipped femoral epiphysis.\nE. Postviral synovitis.\n—_— esses NNN\nMCQ 3.258\nAn infant aged two weeks is noted to be vomiting and losing weight and has recently\nbecome jaundiced. The mother states that her first infant had similar symptoms\nand developed bilateral cataracts. Which one of the following is the most likely\ndiagnosis?\nA. Neonatal diabetes mellitus.\nB. Galactosaemia.\nC. Rubella embryopathy.\nD. Congenital glaucoma.\nE. Neonatal hepatitis.\n|\n} .\n| 323"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.256","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c4c676d26bc7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a176689ccfbc472e6a6e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":341,"source_qid":"3.256"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode