A. Commence sodium valproate.
B. Arrange a sleep electroencephalogram (EEG).
C. Suggest restriction of his evening television viewing.
D. Reassure that these episodes should settle spontaneously.
E. Advise that these episodes are secondary to stresses during the previous day.
MCQ 3.268
A 5-year-old girl was found to have a cardiac bruit wnen she presented with an
upper respiratory tract infection. When reviewed the following week, the murmur is
still present and is grade 2-3/5, mid-systolic in timing, maximal at the left upper sternal
edge. Which one of the following associated features would suggest that her murmur
