A 6-month-old infant is brought into the Emergency Department by her mother. She
has been unwell for three days with initial rhinorrhoea then cough and mild fevers.
Her condition has worsened over the last 24 hours and she is now feeding poorly.
ary On examination she is afebrile but listless with tachypnoea, tracheal tug, intercostal
recession and nasal flaring. On auscultation there are widespread bilateral coarse
crepitations and expiratory wheeze. Which one of the following would be the most
mM likely finding on chest X-ray?
1e','{"A":"No abnormal findings.","B":"Basal consolidation.","C":"Miliary pattern.","D":"Perihilar infiltrates.","E":"Pleural effusion.\n. MCQ 3.282\n. An 18-month-old girl has been vomiting for 24 hours and has had several\nloose stools. Her mother says the child has felt hot and over the last six hours\n= . has been irritable and lethargic. On examination she is lying quietly in her\nmother’s arms. Her temperature is 37.8°C, pulse 110/min, respiratory rate 30/\n] min and her capillary return is 3 seconds. She has a dry mouth and reduced skin\nIg turgor. Which one of the following would be the most appropriate next step in\n~ management?\ns\nA. Intramuscular metoclopramide.\nB. Oral rehydration at home; review in 24 hours.\nC. Oral rehydration in the clinic.\nD. Nasogastric rehydration in hospital.\nE. Intravenous rehydration in hospital.\nSEPT RS AEE AE PY CE STI TST ITT OIE IN TL EIT NCIS NS I NECN BRT TEI I SET PIL ELI INE OA MSIE ESPOSITO\nMCQ 3.283\nA 14-year-old girl is seen because of a dark rash in her axillae and around her neck. The\nrash has been present for several months. She complains of tiredness and is lethargic.\nd She has normal menses which commenced at age 12. She has some abdominal\nif striae and a BMI of 32. Her BP is 120/80mmHg. Which one of the following tests is most\ny likely to establish the diagnosis?\nA. 24-hour urinary cortisol.\nB. Fasting blood glucose.\nC. Serum TSH.\nD. Pelvic ultrasound.\nE. Serum ACTH.\n331"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.281","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b58aad7c5b17","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"05c330db950f1af5ed7d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":349,"source_qid":"3.281"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-