She has been unwell for three days with rhinorrhoea followed by cough and mild
fevers. Her condition has worsened over the last 24 hours and she is now feeding
poorly. On examination she is afebrile, listless and has tachypnoea, tracheal tug,
intercostal recession and nasal flaring. On auscultation there are widespread bilateral
crepitations and an expiratory wheeze. Which one of the following is the most likely
course of her illness?','{"A":"Resolution in 2-3 days.","B":"Improvement in 7-10 days.","C":"Rapid improvement with intravenous antibiotics.","D":"Persistent cough for at least 6 months.","E":"Chronic lung disease.\n\nMCQ 3.295"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[353],"source_qid":"3.293","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b842de4eafa9","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f94149b38efdf76e4397","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":353,"source_qid":"3.293"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_multi_question_group","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"f94149b38efdf76e4397","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":353,"supporting_pages":[353],"source_qid":"3.293","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 10-month-old infant is brought into the Emergency Department by her mother.\nShe has been unwell for three days with rhinorrhoea followed by cough and mild\nfevers. Her condition has worsened over the last 24 hours and she is now feeding\npoorly. On examination she is afebrile, listless and has tachypnoea, tracheal tug,\nintercostal recession and nasal flaring. On auscultation there are widespread bilateral\ncrepitations and an expiratory wheeze. Which one of the following is the most likely\ncourse of her illness?","options":{"A":"Resolution in 2-3 days.","B":"Improvement in 7-10 days.","C":"Rapid improvement with intravenous antibiotics.","D":"Persistent cough for at least 6 months.