j (<5). There is a trace of protein, but no glucose. Culture of her urine shows E. coli 0.1x108
colonies/L. Which one of the following is the most appropriate management?','{"A":"Oral ciprofloxacin.","B":"Parenteral gentamicin.","C":"Oral nitrofurantoin.","D":"Parenteral cephazolin.","E":"No treatment is necessary.\n\nMCQ 3.298"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[354],"source_qid":"3.296","duplicate_group_id":"exact-cedfe852c190","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"dc1a936dd1a76bb13d68","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":354,"source_qid":"3.296"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"dc1a936dd1a76bb13d68","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":354,"supporting_pages":[354],"source_qid":"3.296","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"| A 15-year-old school girl presents for a school health check. She is well. Her examination\nis normal, her BP is 104/68mmHg. A mid-stream urine sample shows leucocytes 2x109/L\nj (<5). There is a trace of protein, but no glucose. Culture of her urine shows E. coli 0.1x108\ncolonies/L. Which one of the following is the most appropriate management?","options":{"A":"Oral ciprofloxacin.","B":"Parenteral gentamicin.","C":"Oral nitrofurantoin.","D":"Parenteral cephazolin.","E":"No treatment is necessary.\n\nMCQ 3.298"},"options_mode":"text","source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_statu