showed almost no liquor was present, and the CTG was normal and reactive. Which
one of the following options is most appropriate regarding her subsequent care?','{"A":"Prophylactic antibiotic therapy should be continued uniil delivery occurs.","B":"Contraction-inhibiting drugs should be administered from now until established\nlabour occurs.","C":"CIG assessments of the fetal heart rate should be repeated weekly.","D":"The white cell count (WCC) and C-reactive protein (CRP) levels should be assessed\nevery 2-3 days.","E":"Labour should be induced now."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[356],"source_qid":"3.299","duplicate_group_id":"exact-41a5a3edd05b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"678aa2c5503c04c1e91f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":356,"source_qid":"3.299"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_multi_question_group","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"678aa2c5503c04c1e91f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":356,"supporting_pages":[356],"source_qid":"3.299","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 25-year-old woman, who lives 50km from the nearest tertiary referral obstetric\nhospital, presents because of premature rupture of her membranes (PROM) at 26\nweeks of gestation, two days ago. This is her first pregnancy andithad been progressing\nnormally until the time the membranes ruptured. No contractions have occurred in\nthe last 48 hours, she has been transferred to the tertiary referral obstetric hospital,\nglucocorticoid therapy has been given, cervical swabs collected, prophylactic\niit antibiotics commenced and ultrasound and cardiotocograph (CTG) assessments\nmade. The cervical swabs showed growth of normal vaginal flora only, the ultrasound\nshowed almost no liquor was present, and the CTG was normal and reactive. Which\none of the following options is most appropriate regarding her subsequent care?","options":{"A":"Prophylactic antibiotic therapy should be continued uniil delivery occurs.","B":"Contraction-inhibiting drugs should be administered from now until established\nlabour occurs.","C":"CIG assessments of the fetal heart rate should be repeated weekly.","D":"The white cell count (WCC) and C-reactive protein (CRP) levels should be assessed\nevery 2-3 days.","E":"Labour should be induced now."},"options_mode":"text","source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["antibiotic","pregnan","prophyl","therapy"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_multi_question_group","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"41a5a3edd05b4fb83b7b9813674ac0af66d923c2","duplicate_group_id":"exact-41a5a3edd05b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"678aa2c5503c04c1e91f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":356,"source_qid":"3.299"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.p